'''''Weigela japonica''''', the '''Japanese weigela''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Caprifoliaceae]]. It is native to southern China and southern Japan, and it has been introduced to the US state of New York, Bulgaria, and probably other locales.<ref name="POWO_150042-1" >{{cite POWO |id=150042-1 |title=''Weigela japonica'' Thunb. |access-date=2 April 2026 }}</ref> A deciduous shrub or small tree reaching {{cvt|6|m}}, it is typically found in scrublands and woodlands at elevations from {{cvt|400|to|1800|m}}.<ref name="FoC_200022528" >{{cite web |url=http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=200022528 |title=半边月 ban bian yue |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2026 |website=Flora of China |publisher=Missouri Botanical Garden & Harvard University Herbaria |access-date=2 April 2026 }}</ref> Its cultivar 'Dart's Colourdream', which reaches {{cvt|2.5|m|ft|0}}, is available from commercial nurseries.<ref name="RHS_151193" >{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/151193/weigela-japonica-dart-s-colourdream/details |title=''Weigela japonica'' 'Dart's Colourdream' Japanese weigela 'Dart's Colourdream' |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2026 |website=Find a plant |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=2 April 2026 |quote=5 suppliers }}</ref>

==Subtaxa==
The following varieties are accepted:<ref name=" POWO_150042-1" />
* ''Weigela japonica'' var. ''japonica'' – southern Japan
* ''Weigela japonica'' var. ''sinica'' {{small|(Rehder) L.H.Bailey}} – southern China

